# The registers tools/gpu_registers_generate.py makes of Linux's headers,
# by block (the module's name), one a line as the header names it without
# "mm" (a register of an index space with its "ix"); "enum NAME" an enum of
# gfx_8_0_enum.h. Each register comes with every field its header gives it.
# Mesa's database (gfx8.mlx, gfx8_enums.mlx) is generated whole and is not
# chosen here; the registers it has in another form than Linux are added to
# gfx_8_0 by the generator itself.
#
# Chosen: every register, field and enum value the engines' files name
# (kernel/gpu_engines.mlx, gpu_smc_sdma.mlx, gpu_compute.mlx,
# gpu_graphics.mlx, gpu_first_space.mlx, tests/support/engine_card.mlx and
# the golden tables' registers), and, ahead of their move, those the
# display's files and the kernel's Vulkan calls name with the header's
# number (gpu_display.mlx, gpu_mode.mlx, gpu_aux.mlx, gpu_ddc.mlx,
# gpu_link.mlx, gpu_plug.mlx, gpu_dpwatch.mlx, gpu_rom.mlx (its two ROM
# words, which it names without the header's "ix"), gpu_ring.mlx,
# gpu_space.mlx). A register is added here and generated, never typed
# (README.md beside this file).

